\newlabel{fig:c31-roads}{{29.1.1}{1715}{Sample 1 of CF 118E. The two rungs \(1\!-\!4\) and \(2\!-\!5\) make every edge lie on a cycle, so the graph is bridgeless and Robbins' theorem guarantees a strong orientation. Sample 2 deletes the rung \(2\!-\!5\), leaving \(1\!-\!4\) a bridge between the two triangles -- the answer flips to \(0\)}{figure.caption.293}{}}
